BT 1 0 0 1 0 46.5 Tm /F1 9.5 Tf 14 TL (This project assessed and hardened a Kali Linux virtual machine using the Lynis security auditing tool. The work) Tj T* (followed a controlled security-hardening cycle: establish a baseline, review Lynis findings, classify) Tj T* (recommendations by risk and applicability, apply selected remediations, verify the resulting system state, and) Tj T* (perform a final Lynis audit.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 57.02362 634.8661 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 46.5 Tm 14 TL /F1 9.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (The initial documented hardening index was ) Tj /F2 9.5 Tf (65) Tj /F1 9.5 Tf (. During the remediation process, the index temporarily fell to ) Tj /F2 9.5 Tf (62) Tj /F1 9.5 Tf  T* (and then recovered to ) Tj /F2 9.5 Tf (63) Tj /F1 9.5 Tf (. After additional targeted remediation and verification, the final documented index) Tj T* (reached ) Tj /F2 9.5 Tf (68) Tj /F1 9.5 Tf (. This represents a ) Tj /F2 9.5 Tf (3-point improvement over the original baseline) Tj /F1 9.5 Tf ( and a 6-point recovery from the) Tj T* (lowest observed score.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
